Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: The most serious cyclobenzaprine (Flexeril) drug interactions are with MAO inhibitors.
MAO inhibitors must never be combined with cyclobenzaprine.
The most serious cyclobenzaprine (Flexeril) drug interactions are also with antidepressants and other serotonergic medicines.
These medicines can cause serotonin syndrome.
Cyclobenzaprine interacts with alcohol and other medicines that cause drowsiness.
This interaction makes sedation worse.
1,2,3
Other medicines and substances that interact with cyclobenzaprine include: 1,2,3
MAO inhibitors such as isocarboxazid, linezolid, phenelzine, rasagiline, selegiline, and tranylcypromine (contraindicated; do not use within 14 days);
antidepressants of any kind, including SSRIs, SNRIs, and tricyclics (risk of serotonin syndrome);
bupropion, tramadol, or meperidine;
verapamil;
alcohol;
opioid medicines, sleeping pills, other muscle relaxers, and medicines for anxiety or seizures;
barbiturates and other CNS depressants;
anticholinergic medicines;
guanethidine or similar blood pressure medicines;
cold or allergy medicines containing an antihistamine.
Triplet: ["Cyclobenzaprine", "interaction causes", "worsened sedation"]

The relation 'interaction causes' in the triplet is defined as 'The interaction between the subject drug and the object entity results in the adverse effect or condition specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
B. 'interacts with': The subject drug has a drug interaction with the drug or substance specified by the object entity that may change effects or cause harm.
C. 'has serious side effect': The subject drug may cause the serious or potentially dangerous adverse effect specified by the object entity that requires medical attention.
D. 'has reporting contact': The subject drug has a designated contact entity specified by the object for reporting side effects or adverse events.
E. 'improves': The subject drug enhances or positively affects the condition or parameter specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
